  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Reliable and Dignified Housing Solutions for Displaced Populations from Donetsk Oblast</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Two years of the large-scale invasion from the Russian Federation that began in February 2022, resulting in enormous immense damage for Ukraine that will be felt over generations.  Recovery and reconstruction needs are estimated at almost USD 486 billion considering an (ambitious) 10-year period to meet them.To this end, with the generous support from Liechtenstein in coordination with central and municipal authorities, the International Organization for Migration (IOM) has developed and proposed the project with the aim to contribute to addressing housing needs of displaced populations from Donetsk oblast by renovating former student dormitories in Dnipro city to become habitational units.</narrative>
  </description>
